<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n84409" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πολέμαρχ-ος</span></b> , ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>chieftain, war-lord,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κνωσίων, Ἀχαιῶν,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				B.
				16.39
			</span></i>, A <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ch.</u>
				1072
			</span></i> (anap.), cf.<i><span class="en">
				<u>Th.</u>
				828
			</span></i> (anap.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> the
			title of high officers in several Greek states: </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b> at Athens, <i>the third archon,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				6.109
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>V.</u>
				1042
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				12.16.10
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				49.7
			</span></i>, al.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὠφληκέναι παρὰ τῷ
			π.</span> in his court, <i><span class="en">
				Lys.
				23.3
			</span></i>; at Sparta, a <i>military commander,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				7.173
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				5.66
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>HG</u>
				4.4.7
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				4.5.7
			</span></i>, etc.; at Thebes, officers of chief rank after the
			Boeotarchs, supreme in affairs of war, ib.<i><span class="en">
				5.4.2
			</span></i> sqq., <i><span class="en">
				<u>Michel</u>
				232
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">ii B.C.</span>, found in Crete), etc.; at Orchomenos, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				7.3175.5
			</span></i>, etc.; at Mantinea, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				5.47
			</span></i>; in Arcadia, <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				4.18.2
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. ἐπιμήνιος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>SIG</u>
					402.1
				</span></i>
			 (Chois, <span class="entity">iii B.C.</span>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> simply, <i>chief, leader,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">συνεφήβων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IG</u>
					22.2055
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
